cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it using the metadata below."

title: "Comparative Analysis of Cis-Regulatory Element Turnover in Drosophila"
type: software

authors:
  - given-names: Jessica
    family-names: Fuchs

abstract: >-
  Computational workflow developed for the analysis of cis-regulatory
  element turnover across Drosophila species. The pipeline integrates
  SCRMshaw-based CRE predictions, orthology information, comparative
  genomic mapping, phylogenetic information, and climate annotations
  to classify and analyze patterns of regulatory conservation and
  divergence.

repository-code: "https://github.com/jessfuchs/cre_turnover"

version: "1.0"

license: MIT

keywords:
  - cis-regulatory elements
  - enhancer evolution
  - regulatory evolution
  - Drosophila
  - comparative genomics
  - SCRMshaw
  - phylogenetics
  - bioinformatics
